---
description: Ensure JSON responses are parsed using strict models rather than raw Maps in the Repository
globs: ["**/*_repository_impl.dart"]
---
# Repository JSON Parsing

**Rule:** Repositories must not parse raw JSON data using `Map` keys directly (e.g. `response['key']`). Instead, they must delegate JSON parsing to Data Models using `.fromJson` methods. This ensures type safety and centralizes the mapping logic within the model layer.

### ✅ Good Example
```dart
@override
Future<UserEntity> login(String email, String password) async {
  final response = await remoteDataSource.login(email, password);
  
  // Use a dedicated model to parse the entire response map
  final authResponse = AuthResponseModel.fromJson(response);

  if (authResponse.accessToken.isNotEmpty) {
    await TokenManagement.instance.saveTokens(
      accessToken: authResponse.accessToken,
    );
  }

  return authResponse.user.toEntity();
}
```

### ❌ Bad Example
```dart
@override
Future<UserEntity> login(String email, String password) async {
  final response = await remoteDataSource.login(email, password);
  
  // Bad: Parsing raw Map directly in the Repository
  final accessToken = response['accessToken'] as String?;
  final userMap = response['user'] as Map<String, dynamic>?;

  if (accessToken != null) {
    await TokenManagement.instance.saveTokens(
      accessToken: accessToken,
    );
  }

  final userModel = UserModel.fromJson(userMap ?? {});
  return userModel.toEntity();
}
```